            "kind": "as_of"
          },
          {
            "name": "deadline_ms",
            "kind": "deadline_ms"
          }
        ],
        "docs": {
          "remote": "    /// Recalls a memory pack.\n    ///\n    /// The lease the engine takes is not a client input, and a bearer slip\n    /// is not one. Embedded, `Effort::High`, `XHigh` and `Max` return the\n    /// engine's `LEASE_REQUIRED`: this client mints no lease. Remote, the\n    /// server admits them on a line of its own and reranks on its `[models]`\n    /// reranker, or runs them unreranked and says so when it has none.\n",
          "ts": "/**\n   * Recalls a memory pack.\n   *\n   * `effort: \"high\"`, `\"xhigh\"`, or `\"max\"` needs a lease this package never\n   * mints: an embedded client returns `LEASE_REQUIRED`; a remote one gets what\n   * the server serves (reranked on its `[models]` reranker, or unreranked and\n   * saying so). `effort: \"call\"` is call mode for live calls: light\n   * effort under a hard deadline (`deadlineMs`, or the vault's call-mode\n   * deadline), answering with the best results ready, marked `partial`.\n   */",
          "py": "Recalls a memory pack.\n\n        ``effort=\"high\"`` needs a lease this package never mints: an embedded\n        client raises ``LEASE_REQUIRED``; a remote one gets what the server\n        serves (reranked on its ``[models]`` reranker, or unreranked and\n        saying so). ``effort=\"call\"`` is call mode for live calls:\n        light effort under a hard deadline (``deadline_ms``, or the vault's\n        call-mode deadline), answering with the best results ready, marked\n        ``partial``. ``format`` takes the engine's exact tokens:\n        ``\"json\"``, ``\"yaml\"``, ``\"toon\"``, ``\"md\"``, ``\"txt\"``.\n        "
        }
      },
      "uniffi": {
        "args": {
          "query": "String",
          "effort": "Effort",
          "scope": "Option<RecallScope>",
          "limit": "u32",
          "format": "Option<String>",
          "as_of": "Option<u64>"
        },
        "output": "MemoryPack"
      }
